    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0694" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.893/7–3047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to General Wedemeyer </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-30">30 July 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83136. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Wedemeyer</hi>: Thanks for 34. It is such
                    a clear picture of the situation that I have passed copies to the President,
                        Leahy,<anchor n="58" xml:id="d563-f1"/> Forrestal<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d563-f2"/> and Petersen.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d563-f3"/> In the
                    Department I have shown it to Lovett<anchor n="61" xml:id="d563-f4"/> and
                        Armour.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d563-f5"/> I want you to know that your
                    approach to the problem has my complete approval. The situation appears most
                    discouraging. If you need anything from this end, please let me know.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d563-f1" n="58" xml:id="d563-f1-content">
                <p>Fleet Adm. William D. Leahy, Chief of Staff to the Commander in Chief, President
                    Truman.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d563-f2" n="59" xml:id="d563-f2-content">
                <p>James Forrestal, Secretary of the Navy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d563-f3" n="60" xml:id="d563-f3-content">
                <p>Howard C. Petersen, Assistant Secretary of War.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d563-f4" n="61" xml:id="d563-f4-content">
                <p>Robert A. Lovett, Under Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d563-f5" n="62" xml:id="d563-f5-content">
                <p>Norman Armour, Assistant Secretary of State for Political Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
